{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791563067,"nonce":"L3lAwmrorGKmRwtDqqDnXd0lDv8=","title":"Port Zyntax's recent Cranelift/MIR-level optimizations that fit WrenLift's Cranelift tier","message":"Zyntax (~/Vibranium/zyntax, 2026-09-26 .. 10-09) runs the same pinned Cranelift (bc2f967). Below, the changes that apply to what 8665161 found in WrenLift's Cranelift loops, in order of fit.\n\n1. Spill-area alignment: 9bc3fcd0, Zyntax issue 7312be0. Cranelift puts register spills right after the explicit stack slots, which it rounds to the word, so a 128-bit spill can sit 8 mod 16, straddle cache lines and lose store forwarding. A zero-sized 16-aligned final explicit slot fixes it without moving slots. Zyntax: FFT -19% on x86-64. WrenLift's q-register spills were at 8 mod 16; done locally (align_spill_area), arm64 unchanged, x86-64 to measure.\n\n2. Invariant store hoisting from counted loops: 0db27ac7. LICM hoists a safely repeated invariant store out of a nonempty counted loop. WrenLift's List store writes elem_class = MIXED on every element; MIXED absorbs, so one store before a loop that stores a Num into that list is equivalent, as long as nothing in the loop can clear the list.\n\n3. Bounds versioning of counted loops: 9e0de451, cbbca5f6, ee471af5, bf665110; Zyntax issue 2abc940. A counted loop whose indices are counter + constant against a bound read before the loop gets a copy where those compares are constants, and the preheader tests once that every index is in range. WrenLift reloads the List count and bounds-checks every access, both reads and writes; for `for (i in 0...a.count)` over a list nothing in the loop resizes, the check is decidable in the preheader.\n\n4. Float pressure across calls: 7bc52ae9 (clif_schedule.rs), Zyntax issue 87f7656. Cranelift's egraph elaboration sinks pure f64 arithmetic past calls to its use, so every operand is spilled across the call instead of one result. A post-egraph pass moves scalar f64/f32 ops back after their last operand definition and before an intervening call. WrenLift's Cranelift bodies interleave helper calls (allocation, dispatch, slow paths) with f64 math, which is the same shape.\n\n5. Error-flag pass: d11c6510, b8f685c0, f43db2eb; Zyntax issue 5caf6de. A dataflow over the error flag decides post-call checks from callee attributes and turns a decided check into a jump. WrenLift polls wlift_error_pending after calls (54840d6 is the compile-time side). Helpers known not to raise (allocation, list count, field ops) need no poll after them.\n\n6. Bounded integer division: fe6cbee0 (bounded_div.rs). Proven ranges give exact multiply/shift quotients and remainders. WrenLift's integer `%` fast path covers fasta (% 139968), pidigits (% 10, / 10), k_nucleotide and reverse_complement (% 1000000007).\n\n7. Known bits for integer compares (5feb4e57) and loop specialisation on stable scalar states (678dc991). These are smaller, and fit after 3.\n\n8. LICM and load CSE aliasing by provenance and exact struct types: 01c106a3, 9a2164e6, fa2f5300, c10d131c. 8665161 #7 found WrenLift's LICM would hoist SubscriptGet/GetField out of a loop that writes the same memory; Zyntax's rules (distinct roots alias only when provenance says so; a load behind a branch stays) are the reference if LICM is to hoist list/field loads.\n\nNot applicable as-is: Python/Lua-specific typing work, drop insertion (refcounting), counter vectorisation (47518ab2, which helps only when LLVM is absent; it may suit the Cranelift tier later).","files":null}]}